/-!
# `L20261018` -- chapters 3 and 4 of the paper, in Lean 4

The library is organised by the paper's own structure:

* `Core/`    the carriers of the paper's objects and the master abstract statements;
* `Ch2/`     the preliminaries of section 2 -- Brauer, Kummer, Hochschild-Serre,
             Hensel / residue map / tame symbol / inertia, Rost-Suslin;
* `Ch3/`     section 3 -- the bi-Kummer structure, the rank barrier, the norm image;
* `Ch4/`     section 4 -- Hensel valuations and ramification in the first slot;
* `Witness/` concrete witnesses discharging the nonemptiness obligations;
* `Infra/`   general cohomological and algebraic infrastructure.

Within a directory the modules are numbered `StepNNN` in the order of the original
development, so reading them in order reads the proof in the order it was built; the
slug after the number says what the step proves.

`DECLARATIONS.md` indexes every declaration of the library by module and line, and gives
the `@source` locator of the module when it formalises a paper item.  `RENAME-MAP.tsv`
maps the historical `HypNNN` module names onto this layout.

This root module imports every submodule, so `import L20261018` is all a downstream file
needs -- the three comparator groups do exactly that.
-/
